  "articleBody": "So, you're ready to tackle that bathroom tile project? That's awesome! But before you jump in, choosing the right professional is super important, especially for areas like showers or if you're working with natural stone. You want someone who really knows their stuff. First off, check for licensing and insurance. This protects you and ensures they're legitimate. Then, ask if they're familiar with the Tile Council of North America (TCNA) methods. This is basically the gold standard for tile installation, so it's a good sign if they know it. Experience with your specific tile or stone material is also a big plus; not all tiles are created equal, and some need special handling. Don't forget to ask about warranties on their work – a confident pro will stand behind what they do. Most importantly, they should be able to give you clear, straightforward answers about how they'll handle waterproofing, especially in wet areas like showers, and how they’ll assess your existing surfaces. If they seem hesitant or can't explain things clearly, that's a red flag. A qualified professional, like the team at HH Remodeling LLC, becomes really vital when you're dealing with sensitive areas, structural concerns, or anything that requires serious waterproofing to prevent future headaches. Don't be afraid to ask those tough questions!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
